      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1248107618,
      "version": 262,
      "versionNonce": 1383278014,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793245998886,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "                AVL Tree\n               -------------\n ( Anderson Velsiki Landis ,Height\nBalanced Tree , Self Balancing Tree )\n===================================\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "                AVL Tree\n               -------------\n ( Anderson Velsiki Landis ,Height Balanced Tree , Self Balancing Tree )\n===================================\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "o6rnT2YbWfsaa5f6apLKB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 137,
      "y": 296,
      "width": 695,
      "height": 500,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1842826814,
      "version": 741,
      "versionNonce": 849959778,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793246496362,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. AVL tree is a balanced Binary Tree .\n\n2. It is a BST which follows special property .\n\n3. The property is that Balanced Factor of every node must be either\n-1, 0 or 1 .\n\n4. If the BF of any node is beyond this range then tree is considered\nas unbalanced and we have to balance it to make it AVL tree .\n\n5. It solve the problem of BST when it is skewed , that is it is either\nheavy on left side or right side and the searching becomes O(n) .\n\nWhat is BF\n==========\n\nBF of a node is the difference between its left subtree height and\nright subtree height .\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. AVL tree is a balanced Binary Tree .\n\n2. It is a BST which follows special property .\n\n3. The property is that Balanced Factor of every node must be either -1, 0 or 1 .\n\n4. If the BF of any node is beyond this range then tree is considered as unbalanced and we have to balance it to make it AVL tree .\n\n5. It solve the problem of BST when it is skewed , that is it is either heavy on left side or right side and the searching becomes O(n) .\n\nWhat is BF\n==========\n\nBF of a node is the difference between its left subtree height and right subtree height .\n\n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "0rs9vBLRrmx-S95CHB-_t",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 147.24299176275133,
      "y": 792,
      "width": 686.5140164744973,
      "height": 459.93534248996644,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1585097790,
      "version": 960,
      "versionNonce": 583634878,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "TmZnXIU9_YbHtsrG5iS-k",
          "type": "arrow"
        },
        {
          "id": "hNvxWin14KImh_MU1QwsQ",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1793250350546,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Steps to create balance tree\n---------------------------------------\n\n1. Start creating the Tree just like BST .\n\n2. After adding each node check its balance factor .\n\n3. If BF is beyond -1, 0 or 1 then the node is considered as critical node\nand the tree is not balanced .\n\n4. Before adding next node we have to make the tree balance .\n\n5. When tree is balanced only then we proceed to add the next node .\n\n\nHow to Balance the tree\n--------------------------------\n\n->    Rotation ",
      "fontSize": 19.365698631156484,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Steps to create balance tree\n---------------------------------------\n\n1. Start creating the Tree just like BST .\n\n2. After adding each node check its balance factor .\n\n3. If BF is beyond -1, 0 or 1 then the node is considered as critical node and the tree is not balanced .\n\n4. Before adding next node we have to make the tree balance .\n\n5. When tree is balanced only then we proceed to add the next node .\n\n\nHow to Balance the tree\n--------------------------------\n\n->    Rotation ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
